eryone's attention  george was the slightly more  level-headed twin who explained what his  brother actually meant fred even passed  george the task of explaining the  marauders map to harry when he could  have done so himself  in fact while harrig was close to both  of the twins he had longer conversations  with george who often explained events  harry might have missed plans he and  fred had or things harry didn't quite  understand fred and george really did  complement each other perfectly  additionally fred was the instigator for  most of their pranks george simply  followed suit whenever the weasley twins  did something particularly naughty it  always seemed to be fred who took the  lead when the twins and ron broke harry  out of privet drive in his second year  it was fred who was driving the flying  ford anglia he was usually the one  behind even the smaller pranks fred was  the one who liberated a salamander from  care of magical creatures so they could  try to feed it filibuster firework and  fred was the one who accidentally  dropped a ton tongue toffee in front of  dudley did you ever notice that it's  always fred and george not george and  fred fred spoke first and george  explained second which almost makes  george's circumstances after fred's  death even sadder the two were  inseparable for their entire lives and  provided that fred was the front man  george was probably quite lost after the  war after years of following the actions  of his twin and never really having to  take action himself  in life they spent nearly every waking  moment together they had a beautiful  friendship and interestingly enough the  books don't really delve much into what  actually happened to george after the  death of his brother losing any kind of  friend or family member is horrendous  but to lose a twin must be soul  destroying after the death of fred what  happened to george in the documentary jk  rowling a year in the life rowling dives  into the weasley family tree and  mentions the following with regards to  george a lot of readers ask me was  george all right and of course he  wouldn't be all right would he that's  the reality but i think that he married  angelina who was actually fred's ex  maybe it's a bit unhealthy but i think  they would have been happy as happy as  he could be without fred i think he  really would have felt like part of  himself died additionally rowling was  asked about george weasley's state in a  2007 interview with bloomsbury how was  george getting along without his twin  well i don't think that george would  ever get over losing fred which makes me  feel so sad however he names his first  child and son fred and he goes on to  have a very successful career helped by  good old ron  the interview also confirms that george  continued working at the business which  he and his brother had created ron  joined george at weasley's wizarding  wheezes which became an enormous money  spinner these are quite tragic answers  from rowling but it's good to see that  she isn't softening the truth losing a  family member is one of the worst things  that we have to deal with in life  effectively yes life would go on for  george but it would never be the same  his companion the person that he had  shared every moment with since childhood  was gone would he be happy again would  he experience joy again yes of course  but would george weasley be changed  forever after the passing of his brother  absolutely so how else did these twin  brothers who were nearly identical in  every way operate as individuals while  fred was a bit more outgoing and  inclined to do a bit of damage him and  george were almost the perfect combo  because george was always there to  mitigate the damage however don't get me  wrong george was happy to do so he would  have never wanted his twins demeanor to  change and was happy to take on damage  control after his brother opened his  mouth fred and george were both  undeniably charismatic but george was as  it were the public face of the weezy  twins able to be much more subtle and  diplomatic than fred george was the twin  who made edits their letter to ludo  bagman knowing that certain wording  would sound accusatory and was the one  who realized why hermione wanted to get  into the school kitchens he was even the  one who remembered to get the new common  room password from a prefect but not  only were their personalities different  they were also unsurprisingly not  identical in athletic performance  athleticism will vary largely on an  individual basis and it just so happens  that george was the better athlete what  game quidditch what position beta while  both fred and george were excellent  beaters and a credit to the gryffindor  quidditch team there were more mentions  of george hitting bludgers than there  were of fred george seemed to be the  slightly more aggressive of the two on  the quidditch pitch described once as  hitting a bludger at a player as a way  of venting his feelings and retaliating  for a foul by elbowing a slytherin beta  in the face  lastly i want to explore if there's a  way to tell them apart physically are  there any key differences that can help  us to spot which one is which this next  part is going to be exploring the  characters from the films as the  real-life actors oliver and james phelps  do in fact have some subtle differences  in their physical appearance for  reference oliver plays george and james  plays fred i got the following  information from a source i've never  heard of online so hopefully it's  accurate  it turns out that george oliver has a  longer straighter and slightly thinner  face the slightly differently set jaw he  also has a mole on the right side of his  neck has slightly more slanted eyes that  are less deep has a slightly longer and  curved nose with a bump has a slightly  crooked smile and is slightly taller  than fred  james fred can be characterized by a  shorter rounder face a scar on his left  eyebrow less slanted deeper eyes a  straight nose and a slightly shorter  stature and i think that about  summarizes all the differences between  fred george did you guys learn something  i know that i didn't know all of this  until researching for the video did  anything surprise you let me know in the  comment section below until next time  remember ask us no questions and will  tell you no lies  [Music]  [Music]  you

